genetics-variant-help-standard = Standard load and effectiveness. Tissue and blood recovery work outside critical condition, starting 30 seconds after the last injury. Does not treat infections, burns or missing organs.
genetics-variant-help-stable = Adds 10 load and reduces complication risk to a quarter. Does not increase effectiveness.
genetics-variant-help-economical = Tissue and blood recovery are 30% slower; nutrition per restored unit is halved. Does not enhance other properties.
genetics-variant-help-temporary = Standard effectiveness. Lasts 20 minutes after adaptation, followed by three minutes of recovery.
ent-DnaVault = DNA archive
    .desc = A medical biodiversity archive with a built-in personal preparation unit.
ent-BiodiversityProbe = biodiversity probe
    .desc = A portable sampler for organisms and harvested plants. Upload its records to a DNA archive.
ent-DnaVaultMachineCircuitboard = DNA archive machine board
    .desc = A control board for a medical sample archive and personal preparation unit.
dna-vault-title = DNA archive
dna-vault-help = Collect samples according to the current requirements and upload the probe. Accepted records leave its memory. Insert an analyzed patient cartridge and select a preparation; a kit with suppressor takes three minutes. Each successful issue clears the collection and assigns new random requirements: 2–5 samples, with different counts for each category. One personal issue per DNA per round; the normal 100 load limit remains.
