virology-lab-treatment = Analysis and medical care
virology-study-next = Next property research takes 90 seconds and requires Medicine 4. Transfer the studied sample to a synthesizer.
virology-study-complete = All properties compatible with this transmission route have been studied.
virology-design-needs-sample = Insert and analyze a sample. Its original family defines transmission and available treatment.
virology-design-profile = Equipment tier: { $tier }. Properties: { $count } / { $max }. Strain budget: { $cost } / { $budget }.
    Incubation: { $incubation } s. Treatment: { $treatment } s. Natural recovery: { $recovery } s.
virology-design-treatment = A basic synthesizer supports one property; a tier four sequencer supports up to three studied properties. Cultures contain 5 units and cost twice the usual biomass. Base family treatment and vaccination cover all variants. Renaming does not bypass immunity. Requires Medicine 4.
virology-culture-label = culture: { $disease }
virology-symptom-fatigue-name = Fatigue
virology-symptom-fatigue-desc = Slightly reduces speed after incubation without increasing direct damage.
virology-symptom-thirst-name = Thirst
virology-symptom-thirst-desc = Adds mild water loss during symptom pulses; fluid replacement remains useful.
virology-symptom-cough-name = Increased coughing
virology-symptom-cough-desc = Slightly increases coughing transmission. Droplet families only; protective clothing still works.
virology-symptom-accelerated-name = Shorter incubation
virology-symptom-accelerated-desc = Reduces incubation by 20% without instant symptoms or faster severe progression.
virology-symptom-persistent-name = Persistent course
virology-symptom-persistent-desc = Increases disease and treatment duration by 20%; base family treatment remains effective.
virology-symptom-quiet-name = Mild early signs
virology-symptom-quiet-desc = Suppresses ordinary symptom popups before severe disease. Analysis still detects infection; incubation is 20% longer.
